# Exact numbers
# Fractions stay fractions; only a root or a trig function makes an approximation.
# meth computes with exact fractions, so there is no rounding error to hunt for.
m:algebra 1/3 + 1/6
m:algebra 0.1 + 0.2
m:algebra 2^100
m:algebra 30!
# A root of a perfect square stays exact, any other root is an approximation (the sign says so).
m:algebra sqrt(16/25)
m:algebra sqrt(2)
# Dividing integers is exact too.
m:algebra gcd(84, 36)
m:algebra lcm(4, 6)
m:algebra 22/7 - pi
# Press F3 on a line to see the steps, if it has some.
